<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!--
        OfficePalette — the whole shared look, in one merge.

        This is the usual choice for a KleiKodesh task pane: tokens, every
        control style, and the implicit aliases that apply them. Merging it
        gives a library:

          - Type tokens: UiFontFamily, FontSizeSmall/Normal/Large
          - Adaptive brush tokens: BgSecBrush, BorderBrush, AccentBrush, ...
          - A keyed style for every common WPF control: buttons and toggles,
            text and password input, text and labels and rules, list and tree
            and tab containers, combo, check and radio, menus and context
            menus, tooltip, slider, progress, expander and group box
          - The look of WpfLib's own UpDownTextBox / UpDownFloatTextBox
          - Implicit styles for all of them except ToggleButton and
            TextBlock, which stay opt-in (via Defaults)

        DO NOT merge this just to get at the tokens or one keyed style. It
        applies a look to roughly two dozen control types. The layers are
        separable, and each is a legitimate thing to depend on:

          Tokens.xaml           colour and type names, NO styles at all.
                                Cannot change how anything looks.
          <Control>Styles.xaml  keyed styles for one control. Take
                                ActionButton without restyling every Button.
          Defaults.xaml         turns the keyed styles into implicit ones.
          OfficePalette.xaml    all of it (this file).

        So a dialog that wants the suite colours and one bordered button
        merges tokens.xaml and buttonstyles.xaml, and is untouched otherwise.

        There is deliberately no implicit ToggleButton at any layer: both
        toggle behaviours are legitimate, so a consumer picks in one line.
        Sizing lives with the consumer too; derive with BasedOn and add
        Width/Height.

        NOTE: Pack URI paths must be all-lowercase (WPF BAML compiler lowercases them).
    -->
    <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/tokens.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/themedcontrol.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/popupstyles.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/updowntextboxstyles.xaml"/>
        <ResourceDictionary Source="/WpfLib;component/themes/defaults.xaml"/>
    </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
</ResourceDictionary>
